    "body": "<div class=\"section-header\">SECTION 2 — Physics</div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">15</span>What is Physics?</h2>\n  <p>Physics is the study of matter, energy, and their interactions.</p>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">16</span>SI Units — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Quantity</th><th>SI Unit</th><th>Symbol</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Length</strong></td><td>Meter</td><td>m</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Mass</strong></td><td>Kilogram</td><td>kg</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Time</strong></td><td>Second</td><td>s</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Temperature</strong></td><td>Kelvin</td><td>K</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Electric Current</strong></td><td>Ampere</td><td>A</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Amount of Substance</strong></td><td>Mole</td><td>mol</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Luminous Intensity</strong></td><td>Candela</td><td>cd</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Force</strong></td><td>Newton</td><td>N</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Energy</strong></td><td>Joule</td><td>J</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Watt</td><td>W</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Pressure</strong></td><td>Pascal</td><td>Pa</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Frequency</strong></td><td>Hertz</td><td>Hz</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Charge</strong></td><td>Coulomb</td><td>C</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Potential Difference</strong></td><td>Volt</td><td>V</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Resistance</strong></td><td>Ohm</td><td>Ω</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Magnetic Field</strong></td><td>Tesla</td><td>T</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Luminous Flux</strong></td><td>Lumen</td><td>lm</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">17</span>Newton's Laws of Motion</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Law</th><th>Statement</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>First Law</strong></td><td>An object at rest stays at rest, and an object in motion stays in motion unless acted upon by an external force. <span class=\"critical\">(Law of Inertia)</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Second Law</strong></td><td><span class=\"critical\">Force = Mass × Acceleration (F = ma)</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Third Law</strong></td><td>For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 6 — LIGHT + SOUND + ELECTRICITY ============ -->\n\n\n  \n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">18</span>Light — Complete Data</h2>\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Speed of Light</strong></td><td><span class=\"critical\">3 × 10⁸ m/s</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Reflection</strong></td><td>Bouncing back of light</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Refraction</strong></td><td>Bending of light</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Dispersion</strong></td><td>Splitting of light into colors</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Scattering</strong></td><td>Spreading of light</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Laws of Reflection</strong></td><td>Angle of incidence = Angle of reflection</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Laws of Refraction</strong></td><td>Snell's Law</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Mirror</strong></td><td>Reflects light</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Lens</strong></td><td>Refracts light</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Concave Mirror</strong></td><td>Converging mirror</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Convex Mirror</strong></td><td>Diverging mirror</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Concave Lens</strong></td><td>Diverging lens</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Convex Lens</strong></td><td>Converging lens</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">19</span>Sound — Complete Data</h2>\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Speed of Sound</strong></td><td><span class=\"critical\">343 m/s (in air)</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Medium</strong></td><td>Sound needs a medium to travel</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Vacuum</strong></td><td><span class=\"critical\">Sound cannot travel in vacuum</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Speed in Solid</strong></td><td>Fastest</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Speed in Gas</strong></td><td>Slowest</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Frequency</strong></td><td>Number of vibrations per second</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Audible Range</strong></td><td><span class=\"critical\">20 Hz to 20,000 Hz</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Infrasonic</strong></td><td>Below 20 Hz</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Ultrasonic</strong></td><td>Above 20,000 Hz</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Echo</strong></td><td>Reflection of sound</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">20</span>Electricity — Complete Data</h2>\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Ohm's Law</strong></td><td><span class=\"critical\">V = IR</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Voltage</strong></td><td>Volt (V)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Current</strong></td><td>Ampere (A)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Resistance</strong></td><td>Ohm (Ω)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Watt (W)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Series Connection</strong></td><td>R = R1 + R2 + R3</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Parallel Connection</strong></td><td>1/R = 1/R1 + 1/R2 + 1/R3</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Conductor</strong></td><td>Allows electricity to pass</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Insulator</strong></td><td>Does not allow electricity to pass</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 7 — PHYSICS PYQ + CHEMISTRY ============ -->"
