    "summary": "Complete exam-ready guide to The Universe and the Solar System.",
    "body": "<div class=\"hero\">\n    <h1>Geography — Complete Notes</h1>\n    <div class=\"hero-sub\">Universe · Solar System · Earth · India · World</div>\n    <div class=\"hero-line\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"legend\">\n    <span class=\"legend-item legend-blue\">📘 Facts</span>\n    <span class=\"legend-item legend-red\">🔴 Firsts</span>\n    <span class=\"legend-item legend-purple\">🧠 Memory</span>\n    <span class=\"legend-item legend-amber\">⚡ Exam</span>\n    <span class=\"legend-item legend-teal\">📌 Revision</span>\n    <span class=\"legend-item legend-green\">✓ Success</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"section-header\">SECTION 1 — The Universe and the Solar System</div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">1</span>The Universe — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Fact</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>Age of Universe</td><td><span class=\"critical\">13.7 billion years</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Our Galaxy</td><td>Milky Way (Akash Ganga)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Type of Galaxy</td><td>Spiral</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Nearest Galaxy</td><td>Andromeda</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Number of Stars in Milky Way</td><td>100–400 billion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Light Year</td><td>Distance travelled by light in one year (9.46 × 10¹² km)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Astronomical Unit (AU)</td><td>Distance between Earth and Sun (149.6 million km)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"memory-box\">\n    <p>Remember the two key distance units:</p>\n    <span class=\"mnemonic\">LIGHT YEAR · AU</span>\n    <p style=\"text-align:center; font-size:11pt;\">Light Year = distance light travels in 1 year · AU = Earth–Sun distance</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">2</span>The Solar System — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>Center</td><td>Sun</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Sun Type</td><td>Star</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Sun's Main Gases</td><td>Hydrogen (71%), Helium (26.5%)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Sun's Surface Temperature</td><td>5,500°C</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Sun's Core Temperature</td><td><span class=\"critical\">15 million°C</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Sun's Diameter</td><td>13,92,000 km</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Sun's Age</td><td>4.6 billion years</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Distance Earth–Sun</td><td>149.6 million km (1 AU)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Number of Planets</td><td>8</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Number of Dwarf Planets</td><td>5</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Asteroids</td><td>Between Mars and Jupiter</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Meteoroids</td><td>Burn up in Earth's atmosphere (shooting stars)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Comets</td><td>Icy bodies that develop tails near the Sun</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"exam-focus\">\n    <strong>Exam Focus:</strong> Sun is a <strong>star</strong>, not a planet. Surface temp is <strong>5,500°C</strong> but core is <strong>15 million°C</strong>. Asteroids lie between <strong>Mars and Jupiter</strong>.\n  </div>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 2 — PLANETS + MOON ============ -->\n\n\n  \n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">3</span>The 8 Planets — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <div class=\"planet-diagram\">\n    <div class=\"planet-row\">\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-mercury\">Mercury<span class=\"p-moons\">0 moons</span></div>\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-venus\">Venus<span class=\"p-moons\">0 moons</span></div>\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-earth\">Earth<span class=\"p-moons\">1 moon</span></div>\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-mars\">Mars<span class=\"p-moons\">2 moons</span></div>\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-jupiter\">Jupiter<span class=\"p-moons\">95</span></div>\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-saturn\">Saturn<span class=\"p-moons\">146</span></div>\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-uranus\">Uranus<span class=\"p-moons\">27</span></div>\n      <div class=\"planet-node p-neptune\">Neptune<span class=\"p-moons\">14</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>#</th><th>Planet</th><th>Type</th><th>Moons</th><th>Key Fact</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Mercury</strong></td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>0</td><td><span class=\"critical\">Smallest</span> · Closest · Fastest</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Venus</strong></td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>0</td><td><span class=\"critical\">Hottest</span> · Earth's Twin</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Earth</strong></td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>1</td><td>Only planet with life · Blue Planet</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>Mars</strong></td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>2</td><td>Red Planet · Olympus Mons</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Jupiter</strong></td><td>Gas Giant</td><td>95</td><td><span class=\"critical\">Largest</span> · Great Red Spot</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td><strong>Saturn</strong></td><td>Gas Giant</td><td>146</td><td>Rings · Least dense</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td><strong>Uranus</strong></td><td>Ice Giant</td><td>27</td><td>Rotates on side · Coldest</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Neptune</strong></td><td>Ice Giant</td><td>14</td><td><span class=\"critical\">Farthest</span> · Strongest winds</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"memory-box\">\n    <p>Remember the planet order (from Sun):</p>\n    <span class=\"mnemonic\">M V E M · J S U N</span>\n    <p style=\"text-align:center; font-size:11pt;\">\"<strong>M</strong>y <strong>V</strong>ery <strong>E</strong>ducated <strong>M</strong>other <strong>J</strong>ust <strong>S</strong>erved <strong>U</strong>s <strong>N</strong>oodles\"</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">4</span>Dwarf Planets — Complete Data</h2>\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Dwarf Planet</th><th>Location</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Pluto</strong></td><td>Kuiper Belt</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Ceres</strong></td><td>Asteroid Belt</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Eris</strong></td><td>Kuiper Belt</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Haumea</strong></td><td>Kuiper Belt</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Makemake</strong></td><td>Kuiper Belt</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"exam-focus\">\n    <strong>Exam Focus:</strong> Pluto was demoted from planet to <strong>dwarf planet in 2006</strong>. Now there are <strong>5 dwarf planets</strong>.\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">5</span>The Moon — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>Type</td><td>Natural Satellite of Earth</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Distance from Earth</td><td><span class=\"critical\">3,84,400 km</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Diameter</td><td>3,475 km</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Time to Revolve Around Earth</td><td>27.3 days</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Time to Rotate on Its Axis</td><td>27.3 days</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Gravity</td><td>1/6th of Earth's gravity</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Atmosphere</td><td>None</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>First Man on Moon</td><td><span class=\"success\">Neil Armstrong (1969)</span></td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 3 — ECLIPSES + EARTH ============ -->"
