    "body": "<h2><span class=\"num\">6</span>Eclipses — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Eclipse</th><th>When</th><th>Result</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Solar Eclipse</strong></td><td>Moon between Sun and Earth</td><td>Sun's light blocked</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Lunar Eclipse</strong></td><td>Earth between Sun and Moon</td><td>Moon's light blocked</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"memory-box\">\n    <p>Remember the order:</p>\n    <span class=\"mnemonic\">SUN · MOON · EARTH (Solar)</span>\n    <span class=\"mnemonic\">SUN · EARTH · MOON (Lunar)</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">7</span>Previous Year Questions</h2>\n  <div class=\"columns\">\n    <p><strong>Q1.</strong> Fastest planet? <em>Mercury</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q2.</strong> Red Planet? <em>Mars</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q3.</strong> Largest planet? <em>Jupiter</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q4.</strong> Earth's Twin? <em>Venus</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q5.</strong> Hottest planet? <em>Venus</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q6.</strong> Planet with rings? <em>Saturn</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q7.</strong> Farthest planet? <em>Neptune</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q8.</strong> Earth–Sun distance? <em>149.6M km (1 AU)</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q9.</strong> Earth–Moon distance? <em>3,84,400 km</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q10.</strong> First man on Moon? <em>Neil Armstrong</em></p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"section-header\">SECTION 2 — The Earth — Our Habitat</div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">8</span>Shape and Size of the Earth</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>Shape</td><td><span class=\"critical\">Oblate Spheroid (Geoid)</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Equatorial Diameter</td><td>12,756 km</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Polar Diameter</td><td>12,714 km</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Equatorial Circumference</td><td>40,075 km</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Polar Circumference</td><td>40,008 km</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Total Surface Area</td><td>510 million sq km</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Land Area</td><td>29% (149 million sq km)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Water Area</td><td><span class=\"critical\">71% (361 million sq km)</span></td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"memory-box\">\n    <p>Earth's land–water split:</p>\n    <span class=\"mnemonic\">29 · 71</span>\n    <p style=\"text-align:center; font-size:11pt;\">29% land · 71% water</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">9</span>Structure of the Earth — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <div class=\"earth-diagram\">\n    <div class=\"earth-layers\">\n      <div class=\"earth-layer earth-crust\">🌍 Crust <span class=\"layer-depth\">0 – 35 km · SIAL / SIMA</span></div>\n      <div class=\"earth-layer earth-mantle\">🔥 Mantle <span class=\"layer-depth\">35 – 2,900 km · Semi-molten rocks</span></div>\n      <div class=\"earth-layer earth-core\">⚛️ Core <span class=\"layer-depth\">2,900 – 6,371 km · NIFE</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"exam-focus\">\n    <strong>Exam Focus:</strong> <strong>Crust</strong> = thinnest + outermost. <strong>Mantle</strong> = thickest. <strong>Core</strong> = innermost, made of <strong>NIFE</strong> (Nickel + Iron). Outer core = liquid, Inner core = solid.\n  </div>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 4 — MOVEMENTS + LAT/LONG ============ -->\n\n\n  \n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">10</span>Movements of the Earth</h2>\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Movement</th><th>Time</th><th>Result</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Rotation</strong></td><td>24 hours</td><td>Day and Night</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Revolution</strong></td><td>365.25 days</td><td>Seasons</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Axis Tilt</strong></td><td>23.5°</td><td>—</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">11</span>Latitude and Longitude</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Latitude</th><th>Longitude</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>Direction</td><td>East–West</td><td>North–South</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Zero Line</td><td>Equator (0°)</td><td>Prime Meridian (0°)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Total Count</td><td><span class=\"critical\">181</span></td><td><span class=\"critical\">360</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Important Lines</td><td>Tropic of Cancer (23.5° N)<br>Tropic of Capricorn (23.5° S)</td><td>International Date Line (180°)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"infobox\">\n    <strong>IST:</strong> 82°30' E (Mirzapur, UP) · <strong>UTC + 5:30</strong>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">12</span>Heat Zones of the Earth</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Zone</th><th>Location</th><th>Climate</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Torrid Zone</strong></td><td>Between Tropics</td><td>Hot</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Temperate Zone</strong></td><td>Between Tropics and Circles</td><td>Moderate</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Frigid Zone</strong></td><td>Between Circles and Poles</td><td>Cold</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <div class=\"memory-box\">\n    <p>Remember heat zones from hot to cold:</p>\n    <span class=\"mnemonic\">TORRID · TEMPERATE · FRIGID</span>\n    <p style=\"text-align:center; font-size:11pt;\">Hot → Moderate → Cold</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">13</span>Previous Year Questions</h2>\n  <div class=\"columns\">\n    <p><strong>Q1.</strong> Shape of Earth? <em>Oblate Spheroid (Geoid)</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q2.</strong> Equatorial diameter? <em>12,756 km</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q3.</strong> Polar diameter? <em>12,714 km</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q4.</strong> Water %? <em>71%</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q5.</strong> Land %? <em>29%</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q6.</strong> Outermost layer? <em>Crust</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q7.</strong> Thickest layer? <em>Mantle</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q8.</strong> Innermost layer? <em>Core</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q9.</strong> Core made of? <em>Nickel + Iron (NIFE)</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q10.</strong> Rotation time? <em>24 hours</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q11.</strong> Revolution time? <em>365.25 days</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q12.</strong> Axis tilt? <em>23.5°</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q13.</strong> Equator? <em>0° Latitude</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q14.</strong> Tropic of Cancer? <em>23.5° N</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q15.</strong> Prime Meridian? <em>0° Longitude</em></p>\n  </div>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 5 — INDIA LOCATION + HIMALAYAS ============ -->"
