    "body": "<div class=\"section-header\">SECTION 2 — National Income</div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">9</span>What is National Income?</h2>\n\n  <p>National Income is the total value of all goods and services produced by a country in a year. It is the most important indicator of a country's economic performance.</p>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">10</span>National Income — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Term</th><th>Full Form</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>GDP</strong></td><td>Gross Domestic Product</td><td>Total value of goods and services produced within a country in a year</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>GNP</strong></td><td>Gross National Product</td><td>GDP + Net income from abroad</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>NNP</strong></td><td>Net National Product</td><td>GNP – Depreciation</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>NDP</strong></td><td>Net Domestic Product</td><td>GDP – Depreciation</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>NI</strong></td><td>National Income</td><td>NNP at Factor Cost</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>PCI</strong></td><td>Per Capita Income</td><td>National Income ÷ Population</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">11</span>Key Formulas</h2>\n\n  <div class=\"quick-rev\">\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>GDP</strong> = C + I + G + (X – M)</li>\n      <li>C = Consumption · I = Investment · G = Government Spending · X = Exports · M = Imports</li>\n      <li><strong>GNP</strong> = GDP + Net Factor Income from Abroad (NFIA)</li>\n      <li><strong>NNP</strong> = GNP – Depreciation</li>\n      <li><strong>NNP at Factor Cost</strong> = NNP at Market Price – Indirect Taxes + Subsidies</li>\n      <li><strong>National Income</strong> = NNP at Factor Cost</li>\n      <li><strong>Per Capita Income</strong> = National Income ÷ Population</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">12</span>GDP vs GNP — Simple Difference</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Concept</th><th>Simple Meaning</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>GDP</strong></td><td>What is produced <em>inside</em> India</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>GNP</strong></td><td>What is produced <em>by Indians</em> (inside or outside India)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>NNP</strong></td><td>GNP minus wear and tear of machinery</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Per Capita Income</strong></td><td>Average income per person</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">13</span>Previous Year Questions</h2>\n\n  <div class=\"columns\">\n    <p><strong>Q1.</strong> What is GDP? <em>Total value of goods and services produced within a country in a year</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q2.</strong> What is GNP? <em>GDP + Net income from abroad</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q3.</strong> What is NNP? <em>GNP – Depreciation</em></p>\n    <p><strong>Q4.</strong> What is Per Capita Income? <em>National Income ÷ Population</em></p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fill-note\">✦ National Income is the single most important indicator of a country's economic health ✦</div>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 4 — BANKING + RBI ============ -->"
