    "summary": "Complete exam-ready guide to Indian Economic Planning.",
    "body": "<div class=\"section-header\">SECTION 4 — Indian Economic Planning</div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">18</span>What is Economic Planning?</h2>\n\n  <p>Economic Planning is the process by which the government sets goals and allocates resources to achieve economic development. India adopted Five Year Plans from 1951 to 2017.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"infobox\">\n    <strong>Inspired By:</strong> Soviet Union (USSR) · <strong>Planning Commission:</strong> Established 1950 · Replaced by NITI Aayog in 2015\n  </div>\n\n  <h2><span class=\"num\">19</span>Five Year Plans — Complete Data</h2>\n\n  <table>\n    <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Period</th><th>Focus</th><th>Result</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>1st Plan</strong></td><td>1951-56</td><td>Agriculture</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>2nd Plan</strong></td><td>1956-61</td><td>Industry</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>3rd Plan</strong></td><td>1961-66</td><td>Self-reliance</td><td><span class=\"critical\">Failed (War)</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Plan Holiday</strong></td><td>1966-69</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>4th Plan</strong></td><td>1969-74</td><td>Growth with stability</td><td>Partial success</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>5th Plan</strong></td><td>1974-79</td><td>Poverty removal</td><td>Partial success</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Rolling Plan</strong></td><td>1978-80</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>6th Plan</strong></td><td>1980-85</td><td>Economic liberalization</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>7th Plan</strong></td><td>1985-90</td><td>Food, work, productivity</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>8th Plan</strong></td><td>1992-97</td><td>Human resource development</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>9th Plan</strong></td><td>1997-2002</td><td>Growth with social justice</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>10th Plan</strong></td><td>2002-07</td><td>Double per capita income</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>11th Plan</strong></td><td>2007-12</td><td>Faster and inclusive growth</td><td><span class=\"success\">Success</span></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>12th Plan</strong></td><td>2012-17</td><td>Faster, inclusive, sustainable growth</td><td>Last plan</td></tr>\n  </table>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<!-- ============ PAGE 7 — NITI AAYOG + BUDGET ============ -->"
